The shapes are in internal/music/music.go by their JSON names. Times are in milliseconds. A Browse is {title, subtitle, imageUrl, description, sections} : with an imageUrl , such as a listener's avatar, it's headed round, as an artist's page is, and description goes under the title a line to each line. A section can hold tracks , albums , artists , playlists , shows , stations , links ( {title, subtitle, imageUrl, page} ), a morePage , and empty , what it says while it holds nothing. A source's first section of tracks leads its Home as a card of the day's songs, which opens a page of all of them, headed by the section's pageTitle if it has one, else its title , and its subtitle after the count of songs. A show's publisherPage is a browse page of who publishes it, which their name on the show's page opens.

An imageUrl can say where its size goes, with {size} , for an image server that makes pictures the size asked: or The app fills in how many pixels across it shows the picture at, 40 in a row and 600 in Now Playing, or 600 where nothing asks for a size. %7Bsize%7D , as JavaScript's URL writes it in a query, counts too. An app older than 0.1.20 fetches {size} as it is, so a plugin that gives it wants a minAppVersion of 0.1.20. Without it, give pictures at about 800 pixels if the service can, rather than as large as they were made: the app fetches and decodes the whole of each, a few megabytes for one thousands of pixels across, to show it in a row.

Of the playlists , those with mine are the listener's own, listed under My Playlists, and the rest are ones they saved. One that is mine and also fixed , such as the songs they liked, is kept by the source itself: the app doesn't offer to rename it, delete it, add songs to it, take them out or move them.

 navigation is the plugin's sidebar, in its order. An entry opens a browse page of its own by page , or one of the app's by builtin : home , liked , savedAlbums , stations or shows , which can be given a title . Without navigation , the sidebar has an entry for each of the app's pages the plugin can do. Up to four stations show as a switch over one card, and more as a grid.

 minAppVersion is the oldest version of MyGo Music the plugin works with. An older one won't install it, and says to update first. Versions before 0.1.8 don't read it.

